        r('(cf. [3], IV)','(cf. [3], III)','quotient reference','The quotient results are in the already checked exposé 212, part III, section 7, notably 7.2-7.4 on pp. 114-115. Part IV, exposé 221, concerns Hilbert and Quot schemes and contains no corresponding group-quotient theorem.','misprint of the original')
        r(r'et définir alors $G^\tau$, $G^\sigma$, $G^\rho$',r'et définir alors $G^\tau$, $G^\rho$, $G^\sigma$','remark, symbol order','The opening definitions make G rho the inverse image of p-primary torsion and G sigma the inverse image of prime-to-p torsion. Interchanging these two names makes them correspond to the following printed descriptions without rewriting those descriptions. For the constant group Z/pZ in characteristic p, G rho=G and G sigma=G zero, directly contradicting the printed order.','misprint of the original')
        r(r'$G_{\mathrm{réd}}$ est un sous-schéma',r'$G^\circ_{\mathrm{réd}}$ est un sous-schéma','first reduced-group name','The subgroup under discussion lies inside G zero and is the denominator G zero reduced of the very next quotient. G reduced need not lie in G zero: a nontrivial constant finite group over a perfect field already contradicts that printed assertion.','misprint of the original')
        r('une fois choisi une clôture','une fois choisie une clôture','algebraic-closure choice','The participle agrees with the feminine noun une clôture.','misprint of the original')
